### `333 say`, and saying from the screen.

say-not-one = there are { $count } of them, numbered 0 to { $last }. "{ $typed }" is not one.

say-no-such = there are { $count } of them, numbered 0 to { $last }. There is no { $index }.

say-not-joined = nobody has handed you the file, so there is nobody to say it to and
    nobody who would count it. `333 join` is the whole of it.

say-already = you already said #{ $index } in epoch { $epoch }. One each, and saying it again would
    not replace it: the first thing a node says is the thing it said.

say-sealing = sealing what you said

say-said = #{ $index } in epoch { $epoch }
    .keyword = said

# Said under the line before, in its column, with no keyword of its own.
say-goes-out = It goes out to everyone this node reaches, and they pass it on.
    Once every 333 minutes you may say one of 333 things, and you say
    it as a number. There is no 334th and there never will be. You cannot
    say it twice, you cannot say it louder, and nobody alive has more to
    say than you do.
    Nobody will tell you what it means, either. There is no table yet, and
    when there is one it will be the same table for all of us,
    untranslated.
    .keyword = {""}

say-given-by-nobody = you hold the file, and nobody handed it to you, so you are on nobody's
    roll and nobody would count what you say. Only a node somebody handed
    the file to may speak: hand it on, and whoever you hand it to can.
